### Pareto Front Assessment

Let me identify the non-dominated experiments (maximizing both Elastic Modulus and Pore Fraction):

| Condition | Modulus (bar) | Pore Fraction | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 14-0add-8deg (run1) | 103.6 | 0.75 | minor creases |
| 14-0add-8deg (run2) | 189.4 | 0.71 | clean |
| 13-0add-20deg | 147.8 | 0.65 | top gap |
| 14p8-0add-17deg | 181.4 | 0.65 | clean |
| 17-0add-13deg (run2) | 354.4 | 0.61 | top gap |
| 17-0add-12deg (run1) | 267.5 | 0.60 | minor wrinkle |
| 17-0add-22deg (run3) | 272.5 | 0.60 | slight top gap |
| 17-0add-18deg | 217.1 | 0.57 | clean |

The **14-0add-8deg** condition (polymer_wt=14, bath_temp=8, pullcast_speed=5, N2, wait=120s, nips=1250s) stands out as the strongest Pareto candidate: run1 gave modulus=103.6, PF=0.75; run2 gave modulus=189.4, PF=0.71. Both are high-pore-fraction results. The run2 result (189.4 bar, 0.71 PF) is particularly compelling — it dominates most other experiments on pore fraction while maintaining competitive modulus.

### Validation Status Check

The 14-0add-8deg condition has two independent synthesis runs:
- **Run 1** (2026-08-28): Modulus=103.6±25.1, PF=0.75±0.02 — minor surface creases
- **Run 2** (2026-10-15): Modulus=189.4±9.3, PF=0.71±0.02 — clean membrane

These are two independent syntheses at the same parameters. The modulus values differ substantially (103.6 vs 189.4 bar), suggesting real run-to-run variability. The pore fraction is more consistent (0.75 vs 0.71). The modulus CV within run2 is low (SD=9.3 on mean=189.4), suggesting the run2 measurement itself is reliable, but the between-run spread is large. A third independent repeat is warranted to better characterize the true mean and variability of this Pareto-front candidate before treating it as confirmed.

### Why This Candidate

- **Pore fraction**: Both runs show PF ≥ 0.71, the highest reproducibly observed in the dataset. No other condition comes close to this level with two independent measurements.
- **Elastic modulus**: Run 2 shows 189 bar — competitive with many other conditions. The between-run spread needs resolution.
- **Membrane quality**: Run 2 was clean and defect-free; run 1 had only minor surface creases.
- **Diversity**: This is a lower polymer concentration (14 wt%) + cold bath (8°C) + N2 + moderate wait region that is undersampled relative to the high-polymer-wt cluster that dominated recent campaigns.
- **Expected learning**: A third run will clarify whether the true modulus is ~100 bar (run 1) or ~190 bar (run 2), and confirm whether PF ~0.70–0.75 is reproducible. This directly informs whether this point is a genuine Pareto improvement.

